// FAEEL derives a tuple involved in modal self-support only when an independent
// foundation exists. founded() is supported both by base() and by
// `possible founded()`; the independent base() derivation makes founded() part
// of the founded extension. Without that derivation, the program still executes
// but the circular tuple is absent. Expect: founded with rows: 1.

#pragma epistemic_mode = faeel

pred base().
pred founded().

base().

founded() :- base().
founded() :- possible founded().

?- founded().
